        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f5c2bbc6-44b1-55aa-a52e-765f45dc4396",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: HeroClix, Attacktix, Shadowrun, Marvel Legends Showdown, XEVOZ, Street Fighter, Gears of War, Halo\n- Companies: WizKids, Toy Biz, Hasbro, Capcom\n- Systems: Clix system\n- Topics: collectible miniatures games, collectible action figure games, fighting video game franchises, superhero comic book universes\n\nFacts:\n- Street Fighter is a fighting video game franchise developed and published by Capcom.\n- HeroClix is a collectible miniatures game that uses the Clix system and centers on superhero comic book worlds, especially the Marvel and DC Comics universes.\n- HeroClix lets players build teams of heroes, villains, or characters from series including Street Fighter, Gears of War, and Halo and battle on grid maps in turn-based play.\n- Attacktix has been compared to HeroClix.\n- Subsequent collectible action figure games included WizKids' Shadowrun, Toy Biz's Marvel Legends Showdown, and Hasbro's XEVOZ and Attacktix.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
